# Paths whose change should prompt a documentation spot-check before shipping.
# REPLACES shipping-work/doc-check.sh's built-in SENSITIVE_PATHS wholesale
# (#318). Tailored together with .skills/doc-sections — tailoring one alone
# yields advice written for a stack this repo does not have (#261, #284).
#
# Entries match path SEGMENTS at any depth and are LITERAL: doc-check.sh quotes
# the entry inside its `case` pattern, so `skills/*/SKILL.md` would match
# nothing. `SKILL.md` matches every skill's; `references/` matches every
# skill's directory. Every entry below matches at least one tracked file,
# which is what keeps the gate off its exit-2 "a list that cannot hit anything
# is not a pass" path.
#
# The defaults this replaces were written for an application repo: they watch
# src/api/, src/models/, schema.sql, composer.json and package.json, none of
# which exist here, and they carry README advice about a top-level CLI list and
# a two-line quick start that this repo does not have either.

SKILL.md
references/
scripts/
docs/
AGENTS.md
README.md
.skills/
tests/structural/
requirements-test.txt
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.github/workflows/
